A shopkeeper marks an article at ₹2,000 and gives a 10% discount. If the cost price of the article is ₹1,500, what is the profit percentage?
A) 15%
B) 20%
C) 25%
D) 30%
Solution : 
    Discount = 10/100 *2000
             = 200

 SP = COST PRICE-Discount
 SP = 2000-200
SP = 1800
profit=1800-1500
profit=300
 profit % = profit/CP *100
 profit=20%

Answer : B
